-The thirteen legacy TC IDs are kept in the legacy order, and each row names either the criterion of this story that the case answers or the slice that owns the legacy case. The Level column follows Template and Rules section R7.2: the legacy level Access maps to Component, and the legacy level System maps to Component where the case side is the contract mock and to End to end where the whole screen is exercised — so the four cases of the read decision are Component here, and the nine case-side cases are End to end and owned by RWB-P3-E1023-APP. In detail: TC-E1-023-11 answers the refused read, which is the one legacy Access case of the key; TC-E1-023-05 answers the out-of-scope page, which is the legacy AC5 and AC-EXC-P4-004-01; TC-E1-023-07 answers the read that cannot be logged, which is the legacy AC7 and AC-EXC-P4-007-03; and TC-E1-023-08 answers the masking by role, which is the legacy AC8 and AC-EXC-P4-004-05 with the identity number and the contact value never clear. The other cases name the case-side slice of the key they belong to: the data from ACE in TC-E1-023-02, the stale batch in TC-E1-023-04, the document hub in TC-E1-023-06, the hold banner in TC-E1-023-09, the empty sections in TC-E1-023-10, the no-copy rule in TC-E1-023-12 and the account link with no ACE row in TC-E1-023-13, all of them RWB-P3-E1023-APP's, with TC-E1-023-01 and TC-E1-023-03 belonging to RWB-P3-E1023-APP and RWB-P5-E1023-APP. No `-ITG` id sits in this story: the integration copy of this key is RWB-ITG-E1023-ITG. The full test, with its Given, When and Then, is in Recovery Workbench Test Cases v7.xlsx, tab Story test cases, under the same test case ID.
